e. economy;

f. culture; and

g. social.

(3) The responsibility of the Regional Government for the protection of the rights of Women as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by:

a. formulation of gender-responsive Regional policies;
b. institutionalization of gender mainstreaming within the Regional Government;
c. empowerment of Women in the political, legal, economic, cultural and social fields in community organizations at the city level;
d. strengthening and developing institutions providing women's empowerment services at the city level; c. implementing prevention efforts against violence against Women.
(4) The responsibility of the Regional Government for the protection of the rights of Children as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by: a . formulation of policies, programs, and Regional development activities with child rights perspective which are set forth in Regional development planning documents;
b. formulation of norms, standard procedures and criteria for assessment of the fulfillment and protection of the rights of Children which refer to the norms, standards, procedures and criteria established by the government;
c. implementation of child-friendly city is carried out in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations; d. facilitation of the implementation of Regional Children's forum; e. increasing community participation in the implementation and protection of the rights of Children; f. monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of programs for the fulfillment and Protection of Children;

I 11

g. guidance of Child Protection institutions; h . providing special protection for Children; and 1. implementing prevention efforts against violence against Children.

