THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF PALANGKA RAYA CITY and

MAYOR OF PALANGKA RAYA

Has Decided REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE.

I II

Article 4

The objectives of Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence include: a. ensuring the fulfillment of rights;

b. providing justice and equality of rights; c. providing protection and security; and d. conducting empowerment.

Article 5

The scope of Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence includes: a. protection of Women; b. protection of Children;

c. coordination and cooperation;

d. responsibilities of Regional Government;

e. community participation;

f. guidance and supervision;

g. evaluation; h. reporting; and

1. funding.

Article 3

Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence is implemented based on the principles: a. responsive to rights;

b. non-discrimination;

c. maintaining confidentiality;

d. empowerment; and

e. participation.

I 11

Article 30

(1) The community is involved in the Protection of Women and Child Victims of Violence.

(2) Community involvement as referred to in paragraph (1) is in the form of participation through prevention, services, empowerment, monitoring, supervision and fulfillment of the rights of Women and/or Children.

I II

(3) The role of the community in the implementation of the Protection of Women and Child Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by: a. providing communication and information through socialization and education regarding the rights of Women and Children;

b. providing suggestions and input in the formulation of policies related to the Protection of Women and Children;

c. reporting to the authorities if there are violations of the rights of Women and Children;

d. playing an active role in the rehabilitation and social reintegration process for Women and Children;

e. forming family partners at the neighborhood/community association or village level by the community;

f. establishing Women and Child Protection units within community organizations and educational institutions;

g. establishment and management of orphanages;

h. establishment of Child rehabilitation facilities; provision of shelters and/or social facilities;

1. vocational skills training; and

J.

k. providing first aid when violations of the rights of Women and Children occur. (4) Further provisions regarding community participation shall be regulated by Mayor Regulation.

Article 13

(1) Fulfillment of Children's Rights as referred to in Article 11 letter b includes: a. guarantee of civil rights and freedoms; b. guarantee of family environment and alternative care;

c. guarantee of basic health and welfare; d. education, leisure time, culture and recreation; and e. special protection.

(2) Special protection as referred to in paragraph (1) letter e, is provided to:

a. children in emergency situations;
b. children in conflict with the law;
c. children from minority and isolated groups; d. children who are exploited economically and/or sexually;
e. children who are victims of narcotics, alcohol, psychotropic and other addictive substances abuse;
f. children who are victims of pornography;
g. children with HIV/AIDS;
h. children victims of kidnapping, sale and/or trafficking;
1. children victims of physical and/or psychological violence; j. children victims of sexual crimes;
k. children victims of terrorism networks;

l. children with disabilities;

I II

m. children victims of maltreatment and neglect; n. children with deviant social behavior; and o. children who are victims of stigmatization from labeling related to their parents' condition. (3) Fulfillment of Children's Rights as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented in order to realize a Child-Friendly City.

(4) Fulfillment of Children's Rights as referred to in paragraph (2) is organized in accordance with the provisions of Laws and Regulations.

