Prevention

Article 16

(1) The implementation of coordination and cooperation on the Protection of Women and Child Victims of Violence aims to:

a. improve efforts to fulfill the rights of Women and Children;
b. improve synergistic and harmonious working relationships; and
c. obtain data and information in the implementation of the Protection of Women and Children.
(2) In order to achieve the objectives as referred to in paragraph ( J) the Regional Government cooperates with: a. other Regional Governments;
b. relevant agencies;
c. non-governmental institutions; d . universities; and
e. community organizations.
(3) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (2) includes:
a. exchange of data and information;
b. socialization or legal counseling lectures; c. rehabilitation of victims of violence; and d. repatriation and social reintegration.

Article 6

